  "notes": "USAGE:\nA compound verb formed from {連|つ}れる (to take along) and {出|だ}す (to take out). Emphasizes the action of bringing someone from one location (typically indoors) to another (typically outdoors).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {外|そと}に{連|つ}れ{出|だ}す (to take outside)\n- {散歩|さんぽ}に{連|つ}れ{出|だ}す (to take out for a walk)\n- {子供|こども}を{連|つ}れ{出|だ}す (to take the children out)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {連|つ}れて{行|い}く: to take along — more general, no emphasis on going outside\n- {引|ひ}っ{張|ぱ}り{出|だ}す: to drag out — stronger nuance of forcing someone out",
